Problem 2: Discount Checker

Ask the user for:

Age
Is the user a student? (true or false)
Conditions:

The user gets a discount if:

Age is 60 or above OR
The user is a student

Use:

||
Example:
Enter age: 20
Are you a student (true/false): true

You are eligible for a discount!

Your condition should be similar to:

if (age >= 60 || student)



SOURCE CODE


import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

     System.out.print("age ");
     int age = sc.nextInt();
     
     sc.nextLine();
     
     System.out.print("Student? (true or false) ");
     boolean student = sc.nextBoolean();
     
     if (age >= 60 || student == true ) {
         
         System.out.print("eligible for a discount");
     } else  {
         
          System.out.print("NOT eligible for a discount");
     }
     
     
    }
}
